      tech: `Consumer and computing milestones of the ${year} era included Digital Equipment Corporation's PDP minicomputers, Philips's compact audio cassette tape, Sony's Trinitron color television picture tube, and Wham-O's 'SuperBall' and Hasbro's original 12-inch 'G.I. Joe' action figures alongside Mattel's 'Hot Wheels' die-cast cars.`,
      pop: `On the ${year} Billboard Hot 100 charts, The Beatles ('Hey Jude,' 'I Want to Hold Your Hand'), The Supremes, Elvis Presley, and The Beach Boys dominated AM transistor radios. At the box office, 'The Sound of Music,' 'Mary Poppins,' 'Goldfinger,' and '2001: A Space Odyssey' packed movie palaces while 'Star Trek' and 'The Ed Sullivan Show' ruled network television.`,
